<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · movement</p><h1 class="enc-title">Expressionism</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as expressionist</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Expressionism was a modernist movement in art, literature and music in the early twentieth century that sought to express emotional experience rather than physical reality. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> it flourished in the work of painters such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egon-schiele">Egon Schiele</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oskar-kokoschka">Oskar Kokoschka</a>, forming part of the cultural brilliance of the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a>.</p></div>
